like-for-like
Same algorithm and the same 32-element working arrays. The reference's loop/return are state machines (the language has no break) and x >> 1 is x / 2 (values are never negative). Other stores are checked and undo-logged. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: perm1, perm, count) is declared `unlogged`, kept out of the undo log.
